alues\ndistinct_values = set()\nfor expr in expressions:\n    distinct_values.add(expr)\n\n# The number of distinct values\nnum_distinct_values = len(distinct_values)\nprint(num_distinct_values)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe output indicates that there is only one distinct value for the expression \\(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5 + 1\\) when parentheses are inserted in different ways. This value is 121, which is the result of the expression without any parentheses and also the result of any expression with parentheses inserted in any valid way.\n\nTo confirm, let's list the distinct values explicitly:\n\n1. \\((2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n2. \\((2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 20) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n3. \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 12 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n4. \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5))) + 1 = (2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 20)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 60) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n5. \\(((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5 + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5 + 1 = (6 \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5 + 1 = 24 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n6. \\(((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (6 \\cdot 20) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n7. \\(((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)) \\cdot 5) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 12) \\cdot 5) + 1 = (24 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n8. \\(((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)))) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 20))) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 60)) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n9. \\((2 \\cdot ((3 \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot ((3 \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot (12 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 60) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n10. \\((2 \\cdot ((3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)))) + 1 = (2 \\cdot ((3 \\cdot 20))) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 60) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n11. \\(((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (6 \\cdot 20) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n12. \\(((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)) \\cdot 5) + 1 = ((2 \\cdot 12) \\cdot 5) + 1 = (24 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121