rac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\n   \\]\n\n4. Find a common denominator to combine the fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x}\n   \\]\n\n5. Use the Pythagorean identity \\(\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\) to simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\n   \\]\n\n6. The expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x\n   \\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's verify this step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols('x')\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = simplify(expr)\n\n# Print the simplified expression\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\) is indeed \\(\\cot x\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\cot x}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we will first rewrite the expression using the definitions of the trigonometric functions. Recall that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\). So, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we will find a common denominator to combine these two terms. The common denominator is \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n\\]\n\nWe know from the Pythagorean identity that \\(1 - \