rees. This means that after every 360 degrees, the skater will be facing the same direction she started in.\n\n2. **Calculate the number of full rotations**: We need to find out how many full 360-degree rotations are in 2250 degrees. We do this by dividing 2250 by 360.\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater has completed 6 full rotations and an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Determine the remaining angle**: To find the remaining angle after the full rotations, we multiply 0.25 by 360 degrees.\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\times 360 = 90\n   \\]\n   So, after 6 full rotations, the skater has an additional 90 degrees to spin.\n\n4. **Determine the final direction**: The skater started facing north. After spinning 90 degrees to her right, she will be facing east. This is because:\n   - 0 degrees (or 360 degrees) is north\n   - 90 degrees is east\n   - 180 degrees is south\n   - 270 degrees is west\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the skater will be facing \\boxed{east}.', 'To solve this problem, we need to understand how rotations work and how they relate to the directions. A full rotation is 360 degrees, and after every full rotation, the figure skater will be facing the same direction she started in. So, we need to find the equivalent angle after reducing 2250 degrees by full rotations (multiples of 360 degrees).\n\nHere\'s the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Calculate the equivalent angle by finding the remainder when 2250 is divided by 360.\n2. Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle.\n\nLet\'s do this step-by-step in Python:\n\n1. Calculate the remainder of 2250 divided by 360.\n2. Determine the direction based on the remainder.\n\nLet\'s implement this in code.\n```python\n# Calculate the equivalent angle after full rotations\nangle = 2250 % 360\n\n# Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle\nif angle == 0:\n    direction = "north"\nelif angle == 90:\n    direction = "east"\nelif angle == 180:\n    direction = "south"\nelif angle == 270:\n    direction = "west"\nelse:\n    direction = "north"  # This is a default case, but it will never be used since the angle will be one of the exact multiples of 90\n\nprint((angle, direction))\n```\n```output\n(90, \'east\')\n```\nThe equivalent angle after reducing 2250 degrees by full rotations is 90 degrees. Therefore, the figure skater is facing east when she finishes her spin.\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{east}}\\).', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the starting position:**\n   - The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of full rotations:**\n   - A full rotation is 360 degrees.\n   - Divide 2250 degrees by 360 degrees to find out how many full rotations she completes:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{2250}{360} = 6.25\n     \\]\n   - This means she completes 6 full rotations and has an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Determine the remaining angle after full rotations:**\n   - Multiply the decimal part of the rotation (0.25) by 360 degrees to find the remaining angle:\n     \\[\n     0.25 \\times 360 = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n     \\]\n   - So, after 6 full rotations, she has an additional 90 degrees to spin.\n\n4. **Determine the direction after the remaining angle:**\n   - Starting from north and spinning 90 degrees to the right:\n     - North to East (90 degrees clockwise)\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Calculate the effective rotation:**\n   Since a full rotation is 360 degrees, we need to find the equivalent angle within one full rotation by subtracting multiples of 360 degrees from 2250 degrees.\n\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6.25\n   \\]\n\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Convert the decimal part to degrees:**\n   To find the additional degrees beyond the full rotations:\n\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\times 360 = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n   So, the skater has spun an additional 90 degrees beyond 6 full rotations.\n\n4. **Determine the final direction:**\n   Starting from north and spinning 90 degrees to the right (clockwise) will bring the skater to face east.\n\nTherefore, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}} when she finishes her spin.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Determine the total degrees in a full circle:**\n   A full circle is 360 degrees.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of full circles in 2250 degrees:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2250 \\text{ degrees}}{360 \\text{ degrees/circle}} = 6.25 \\text{ circles}\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full circles and an additional 0.25 of a circle.\n\n4. **Calculate the degrees in the additional 0.25 of a circle:**\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\times 360 \\text{ degrees} = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the direction after the additional 90 degrees:**\n   - Starting from north, spinning 90 degrees to the right (clockwise) will face the skater east.\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the figure skater will be facing \\boxed{\\text{east}}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial position:**\n   - The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Convert the total degrees into full rotations:**\n   - A full rotation is 360 degrees.\n   - We need to find out how many full rotations and the remaining degrees 