. We need to find out how many full rotations are in 2250 degrees.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of full rotations} = \\frac{2250 \\text{ degrees}}{360 \\text{ degrees/rotation}} = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Calculate the remaining degrees after full rotations**: \n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining degrees} = 2250 \\text{ degrees} - (6 \\times 360 \\text{ degrees}) = 2250 \\text{ degrees} - 2160 \\text{ degrees} = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n   So, after 6 full rotations, the skater has an additional 90 degrees to spin.\n\n4. **Determine the final direction**: Starting from north and spinning 90 degrees to the right (clockwise), the skater will face east.\n\nTherefore, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}} when she finishes her spin.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Convert the total degrees into full rotations:**\n   A full rotation is 360 degrees. We need to find out how many full rotations and the remaining degrees are in 2250 degrees.\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and has an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Calculate the degrees in the remaining rotation:**\n   To find the remaining degrees, multiply the decimal part by 360:\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\times 360 = 90\n   \\]\n   So, the skater spins an additional 90 degrees.\n\n4. **Determine the final direction:**\n   Starting from north, a 90-degree spin to the right will face the skater east.\n\nTherefore, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}} when she finishes her spin.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction**: The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. *