e the known angles and solve for \\(\\alpha\\):\n   \\[\n   215^\\circ + \\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma + \\delta = 720^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma + \\delta = 505^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n6. **Use the Property of Cyclic Hexagons:**\n   In a cyclic hexagon, the opposite angles sum to \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha + \\beta = 180^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\gamma + \\delta = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n7. **Solve for \\(\\alpha\\):**\n   Substitute the values:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha + (180^\\circ - \\beta) = 505^\\circ - 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\alpha + 180^\\circ - \\beta = 325^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\alpha - \\beta = 145^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nSince we don't have enough information to determine \\(\\beta\\) directly, we can use the fact that the sum of the angles in a cyclic hexagon can be used to find \\(\\alpha\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python to verify the calculations and find the measure of \\(\\alpha\\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nalpha, beta, gamma, delta = sp.symbols('alpha beta gamma delta')\n\n# Given angles\nangle_F = 105\nangle_B = 110\n\n# Sum of the interior angles of the hexagon\nsum_of_angles = 720\n\n# Equation for the sum of the angles\neq1 = sp.Eq(angle_F + angle_B + alpha + beta + gamma + delta, sum_of_angles)\n\n# Opposite angles in a cyclic hexagon\neq2 = sp.Eq(alpha + beta, 180)\neq3 = sp.Eq(gamma + delta, 180)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (alpha, beta, gamma, delta))\n\n# Extract the value of alpha\nalpha_value = solution[alpha]\nprint(alpha_value)\n```\n```output\n325 - delta\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the setup of the equations. Let's re-evaluate the problem and correct the approach.\n\nGiven:\n- The sum of the interior angles of a hexagon is \\(720^\\circ\\).\n- Two angles are given: \\(105^\\circ\\) at vertex \\(F\\) and \\(110^\\circ\\) at vertex \\(B\\).\n\nWe need to find the measure of angle \\(\\alpha\