te values change sign are \\( x = -5 \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). These points divide the number line into three intervals: \\( x < -5 \\), \\( -5 \\le x < 2 \\), and \\( x \\ge 2 \\). We will analyze the equation in each of these intervals.\n\n1. **Case 1: \\( x < -5 \\)**\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = -(x+5) = -x-5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = -(3x-6) = -3x+6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   -x-5 - (-3x+6) = 0 \\implies -x-5 + 3x-6 = 0 \\implies 2x-11 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{11}{2}\n   \\]\n   Since \\( \\frac{11}{2} \\) is not less than \\(-5\\), this solution is not valid for this case.\n\n2. **Case 2: \\( -5 \\le x < 2 \\)**\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = x+5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = -(3x-6) = -3x+6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   x+5 - (-3x+6) = 0 \\implies x+5 + 3x-6 = 0 \\implies 4x-1 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n   Since \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\) is between \\(-5\\) and \\(2\\), this solution is valid.\n\n3. **Case 3: \\( x \\ge 2 \\)**\n   \\[\n   |x+5| = x+5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad |3x-6| = 3x-6\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   x+5 - (3x-6) = 0 \\implies x+5 - 3x+6 = 0 \\implies -2x+11 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{11}{2}\n   \\]\n   Since \\( \\frac{11}{2} \\) is greater than or equal to \\(2\\), this solution is valid.\n\nAmong the valid solutions, the largest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\( \\frac{11}{2} \\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{2}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the equation |x+5| - |3x-6| = 0\ndef check_equation(x):\n    return abs(x + 5) - abs(3 * x - 6)\n\n# Check the solutions in the different intervals\nsolutions = []\n\n# Case 1: x < -5\n# We already know from the reasoning that x = 11/2 is not valid in this interval\n\n# Case 2: -5 <= x < 2\nx1 = 1 / 4\nif check_equation(x1) == 0:\n    solutions.append(x1)\n\n# Case 3: x >= 2\nx2 = 11 / 2\nif check_equation(x2) == 0:\n    solutions.append(x2)\n\n# Find the larges