os 80^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\cos 80^\\circ - 1}{\\cos 80^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the expression further:**\n   We need to find a way to simplify \\(\\frac{4 \\cos 80^\\circ - 1}{\\cos 80^\\circ}\\). We can use the fact that \\(\\cos 80^\\circ = \\sin 10^\\circ\\) and \\(\\sin 80^\\circ = \\cos 10^\\circ\\). So we need to find a way to express \\(4 \\cos 80^\\circ - 1\\) in a simpler form.\n\n4. **Use the identity \\(\\cos 3\\theta = 4 \\cos^3 \\theta - 3 \\cos \\theta\\):**\n   Let \\(\\theta = 20^\\circ\\), then \\(\\cos 60^\\circ = 4 \\cos^3 20^\\circ - 3 \\cos 20^\\circ\\). Since \\(\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2} = 4 \\cos^3 20^\\circ - 3 \\cos 20^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\cos^3 20^\\circ - 3 \\cos 20^\\circ - \\frac{1}{2} = 0\n   \\]\n   This is a cubic equation in \\(\\cos 20^\\circ\\). We can use this to find a relationship between \\(\\cos 80^\\circ\\) and \\(\\cos 20^\\circ\\).\n\n5. **Simplify the expression using the identity:**\n   We can use the fact that \\(\\cos 80^\\circ = \\cos (60^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\cos 60^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 60^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} \\cos 20^\\circ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\sin 20^\\circ\\).\n\n6. **Final simplification:**\n   Using the identity \\(\\cos 80^\\circ = \\sin 10^\\circ\\) and \\(\\sin 80^\\circ = \\cos 10^\\circ\\), we can simplify the expression to:\n   \\[\n   \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\cos 80^\\circ - 1}{\\cos 80^\\circ}\\right) = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\sin 10^\\circ - 1}{\\sin 10^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(4 - \\frac{1}{\\sin 10^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\sin 10^\\circ - 1}{\\sin 10^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\sin 10^\\circ - 1}{\\sin 10^\\circ}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\sin 80^\\circ \\left(\\frac{4 \\sin 10^\\circ - 1}{\\sin 10^\\c