s of an arithmetic sequence. In an arithmetic sequence, the difference between consecutive terms is constant. Let's denote the first term of the sequence by \\(a\\) and the common difference by \\(d\\).\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be expressed as:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\n\nGiven:\n- The fourth term \\(a_4 = 200\\)\n- The eighth term \\(a_8 = 500\\)\n\nWe can set up the following equations based on the given information:\n\\[ a + 3d = 200 \\]\n\\[ a + 7d = 500 \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the sixth term \\(a_6\\), which is given by:\n\\[ a_6 = a + 5d \\]\n\nFirst, we will solve the system of equations to find \\(a\\) and \\(d\\). Then we will use these values to find \\(a_6\\).\n\nLet's solve the system of equations step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the symbols\na, d = symbols('a d')\n\n# Define the equations based on the given information\neq1 = Eq(a + 3*d, 200)\neq2 = Eq(a + 7*d, 500)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (a, d))\na_value = solution[a]\nd_value = solution[d]\n\n# Calculate the sixth term\na_6 = a_value + 5*d_value\nprint((a_value, d_value, a_6))\n```\n```output\n(-175, 125, 375)\n```\nThe solution to the system of equations gives us the values:\n\\[ a = -175 \\]\n\\[ d = 125 \\]\n\nUsing these values, we can find the sixth term of the arithmetic sequence:\n\\[ a_6 = a + 5d = -175 + 5 \\cdot 125 = -175 + 625 = 375 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sixth term of the arithmetic sequence is \\(\\boxed{375}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of arithmetic sequences. In an arithmetic sequence, the difference between consecutive terms is constant. Let's denote the first term of the sequence by \\(a\\) and the common difference by \\(d\\).\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be expressed as:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\n\nGiven:\n- The fourth term \\(a_4 = 200\\)\n- The eighth term \\(a_8 = 500\\)\n\nWe can set up 