ac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n3. Now we need to find the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\): \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n4. Finally, we need to find the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\): \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{1 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo the final simplified expression is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Innermost expression\r\ninner_expr = sqrt(Rational(1, 729))\r\n\r\n# Next step: cube root of the inner expression\r\ncube_root_expr = inner_expr**(Rational(1, 3))\r\n\r\n# Final step: square root of the cube root expression\r\nfinal_expr = sqrt(cube_root_expr)\r\n\r\n# Rationalize the denominator\r\nrationalized_expr = final_expr.simplify()\r\nprint(rationalized_expr)\n```\n```output\nsqrt(3)/3\n```\nThe simplified expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is indeed \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we can break it down step by step.\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression: \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then take the cube root of the result.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's do this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we can calculate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\). This is the same as \\(\\left(\\frac{1}{729}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\).\n\nNext, we take the cube root of the result, which is the same as raising it to the power of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\nFinally, we take the square root of the result from the previous step, which is the same as raising it to the power of \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nLet's cal