e expression $\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}$, we will break it down step by step.\n\n1. First, simplify the innermost expression $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}$.\n2. Then, take the cube root of the result from step 1.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's do this step by step.\n\n1. Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\n   \\]\n2. Take the cube root of $\\frac{1}{27}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n3. Take the square root of $\\frac{1}{3}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\n   \\]\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n   \\]\n\nSo the final simplified expression is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpr = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\r\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe numerical value of the expression $\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}$ is approximately $0.577350269189626$. This is the decimal representation of $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we need to work from the inside out.\n\n1. First, simplify the innermost expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then, take the cube root of the result.\n3. Finally, take the square root of that result.\n\nLet's break it down step by step.\n\n1. The innermost expression is \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\). We know that \\(729 = 3^6\\), so \\(\\frac{1}{729} = \\frac{1}{3^6} = 3^{-6}\\). Taking the square root of \\(3^{-6}\\) gives us \\(3^{-3} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\n2. Next, we take the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\). Since \\(27 = 3^3\\), \\(\\frac{1}{27} = \\frac{1}{3^3} = 3^{-3}\\). Taking the cube root of \\(3^{-3}\\) gives us \\(3^{-1} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\n3. Finally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\). This is \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\). To rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\), which gives us \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo the final simplified expression is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\nprint(simplified_expr)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe numerical value of the simplified expression \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) is approximately \\(0.577350269189626\\), which confirms our symbolic simplification.\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\).", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we will break it down step-by-step.\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Take the cube root of the result from step 1.\n3. Take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's simplify it step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we note that \\(\\frac{1}{729}\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{1}{3^6}\\). So, \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3^6}} = \\frac{1}{3^3} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\nNext, we take the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\). Since \\(\\frac{1}{27} = \\frac{1}{3^3}\\), the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\nFinally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), which is \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\). To rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\), giving us \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\n\n# Rationalize the denominator\nrationalized_expr = sp.together(simplified_expr)\n\nprint(rationalized_expr)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe output \\(0.577350269189626\\) is the numerical value of \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\). Therefore, the simplified form of the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is indeed \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we need to break it down step by step.\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression: \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then take the cube root of the result.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\left(\\frac{1}{729}\\right)^{1/2} = \\frac{1}{27}\\) because \\(729 = 27^2\\).\n2. \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\left(\\frac{1}{27}\\right)^{1/3} = \\frac{1}{3}\\) because \\(27 = 3^3\\).\n3. \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{1/2} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo the final simplified expression is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nexpression = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\n\n# Rationalize the denominator\nrationalized_expression = sp.together(simplified_expression)\n\nprint(rationalized_expression)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe numerical value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is approximately \\(0.577350269189626\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the expression step by step. The expression given is:\n\n$$\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}$$\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression: $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}$.\n2. Then take the cube root of the result from step 1.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's do this step by step.\n\n1. Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, take the cube root of $\\frac{1}{27}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. Finally, take the square root of $\\frac{1}{3}$:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\n   \\]\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n   \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\n\n# Rationalize the denominator\nrationalized_expr = sp.together(simplified_expr)\n\nprint(rationalized_expr)\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\). Let's break it down step-by-step.\n\n1. First, simplify the innermost expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then, take the cube root of the result from step 1.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's start with the innermost expression. The square root of \\(\\frac{1}{729}\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}}\\). Since \\(729 = 27^2\\), we have \\(\\sqrt{729} = 27\\), so \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\nNext, we take the cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\). Since \\(27 = 3^3\\), we have \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\nFinally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\). This gives us \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's verify this step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\r\n\r\n# Rationalize the denominator\r\nrationalized_expression = sp.together(simplified_expression)\r\n\r\nprint(rationalized_expression)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe numerical value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\) is approximately \\(0.577350269189626\\). This is the decimal representation of \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nSo the final answer in LaTeX format is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. First, simplify the innermost expression, which is \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then, take the cube root of the result from step 1.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's break this down step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\)\nThe square root of \\(\\frac{1}{729}\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}}\\). Since \\(729 = 27^2\\), \\(\\sqrt{729} = 27\\). So, \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\n### Step 2: Simplify \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}}\\)\nThe cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\) is \\(\