 - n \\]\n\nNext, we substitute this expression for \\( d \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 10(11 - n) + 5n = 75 \\]\n\nNow we can solve for \\( n \\):\n\\[ 110 - 10n + 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 75 = 5n \\]\n\\[ 35 = 5n \\]\n\\[ n = 7 \\]\n\nSo, Hillary has 7 nickels. We can verify this by finding the number of dimes:\n\\[ d = 11 - n = 11 - 7 = 4 \\]\n\nThen we check the total value:\n\\[ 10d + 5n = 10(4) + 5(7) = 40 + 35 = 75 \\]\n\nThe solution satisfies both equations, so the number of nickels is indeed 7. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Let's define the total number of coins and the total value in cents\ntotal_coins = 11\ntotal_value = 75\n\n# We will iterate over possible values of n (number of nickels)\nfor n in range(total_coins + 1):\n    d = total_coins - n  # number of dimes\n    if 10 * d + 5 * n == total_value:\n        number_of_nickels = n\n        break\n\nprint(number_of_nickels)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe number of nickels Hillary has is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).", "Let's solve this problem step by step. We'll use algebra to set up the equations and then use Python to solve them.\n\n1. Let \\( d \\) be the number of dimes.\n2. Let \\( n \\) be the number of nickels.\n\nFrom the problem, we have the following two equations:\n1. \\( d + n = 11 \\) (since there are a total of 11 coins)\n2. \\( 10d + 5n = 75 \\) (since the total value of the coins is 75 cents)\n\nWe can solve these equations step by step. First, we can express \\( d \\) in terms of \\( n \\) from the first equation:\n\\[ d = 11 - n \\]\n\nNext, we substitute this expression for \\( d \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 10(11 - n) + 5n = 75 \\]\n\nNow we can solve for \\( n \\):\n\\[ 110 - 10n + 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 75 = 5n \\]\n\\[ 35 = 5n \\]\n\\[ n = 7 \\]\n\nSo, Hillary has 7 nickels. Let's verify this by calculating the number of dimes and the total value:\n\\[ d = 11 - n = 11 - 7 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 10d + 5n = 10(4) + 5(7) = 40 + 3