d{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nNow we can find $\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ using the linearity of $\\mathbf{A}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = -1 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = -1 \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]", "To find the matrix $\\mathbf{A}$, we can use the given information to set up a system of linear equations. Let $\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & i \\end{pmatrix}$. Then we have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a + b \\\\ 3d + e \\\\ 3g + h \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -5a + 2b + 2c \\\\ -5d + 2e + 2f \\\\ -5g + 2h + 2i \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n3a + b = 2 \\\\\n3d + e = 4 \\\\\n3g + h = -3 \\\\\n-5a + 2b + 2c = 0 \\\\\n-5d + 2e + 2f = -5 \\\\\n-5g + 2h + 2i = -5\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nWe can solve this system of equations to find the values of $a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h,$ and $i$. Once we have the matrix $\\mathbf{A}$, we can then compute $\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$.\nLet's use Python to solve this system of equations and find the matrix $\\mathbf{A}$.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variables\na, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i = symbols('a b c d e f g h