r with two different toppings from a selection of 8, we need to calculate the number of combinations of 8 toppings taken 2 at a time. This is because the order in which the toppings are chosen does not matter.\n\nThe formula for combinations is given by:\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}\n\\]\nwhere \\( n \\) is the total number of items to choose from, \\( r \\) is the number of items to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes factorial, which is the product of all positive integers up to that number.\n\nIn this problem, \\( n = 8 \\) and \\( r = 2 \\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8!}{2!(8-2)!} = \\frac{8!}{2!6!}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the factorials. Recall that \\( 8! = 8 \\times 7 \\times 6! \\). The \\( 6! \\) terms cancel out in the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8 \\times 7 \\times 6!}{2! \\times 6!} = \\frac{8 \\times 7}{2!}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\( 2! \\), which is \\( 2 \\times 1 = 2 \\):\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8 \\times 7}{2} = \\frac{56}{2} = 28\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different pizzas Mikka could order is \\(\\boxed{28}\\).', "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways Mikka can choose 2 toppings out of 8 available toppings. This is a combination problem because the order in which he chooses the toppings does not matter.\n\nThe formula for combinations is given by:\n\n$$\n\\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}\n$$\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the total number of items to choose from, \\( r \\) is the number of items to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes the factorial, which is the product of all positive integers up to that number.\n\nFor Mikka's pizza, we have:\n\n- \\( n = 8 \\) (the total number of toppings)\n- \\( r = 2 \\) (the number of toppings to choose)\n\nPlugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n$$\n\\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8!}{2!(8-2)!}\n$$\n\nFirst, calculate the factorials:\n\n$$\n8! = 8 \\times 7 \\times 6 \\times 5 \\times 4 \