n \\(x=4\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 4\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression step by step.\n\nLet's start by substituting \\(x = 4\\) into the expression:\n\n\\[\n(3 \\cdot 4 - 2)(4 \\cdot 4 + 1) - (3 \\cdot 4 - 2) \\cdot 4 \\cdot 4 + 1\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(12 - 2)(16 + 1) - (12 - 2) \\cdot 16 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n10 \\cdot 17 - 10 \\cdot 16 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n170 - 160 + 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of the expression when \\(x = 4\\) is \\(11\\). Let's confirm this by running the code.\n```python\n# Define the expression as a function\ndef expression_value(x):\n    return (3*x - 2)*(4*x + 1) - (3*x - 2)*4*x + 1\n\n# Substitute x = 4 into the expression\nresult = expression_value(4)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe value of the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\) when \\(x=4\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1) - (3x-2)4x + 1\\) when \\(x = 4\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 4\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression step by step.\n\nLet's break it down and compute it using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we'll substitute \\(x = 4\\) into the expression and then simplify it:\n\n1. \\((3 \\cdot 4 - 2)(4 \\cdot 4 + 1) - (3 \\cdot 4 - 2) \\cdot 4 \\cdot 4 + 1\\)\n2. Simplify the expression inside the parentheses first:\n   - \\(3 \\cdot 4 - 2 = 12 - 2 = 10\\)\n   - \\(4 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 16 + 1 = 17\\)\n   - So the expression becomes \\(10 \\cdot 17 - 10 \\cdot 16 + 1\\)\n3. Now we can simplify further:\n   - \\(10 \\cdot 17 = 170\\)\n   - \\(10 \\cdot 16 = 160\\)\n   - So the expression becomes \\(170 - 160 + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11\\)\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 4\n\n# Calculate the expression step by step\nterm1 = (3 * x - 2) * (4 * x + 1)\nterm2 = (3 * x - 2) * 4 * x\nresult = term1 - term2 + 1\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe value of the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+