:\n\\[ \\frac{p(3)}{p(4)} = \\frac{-10}{-11} = \\frac{10}{11} \\]\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{10}{11}} \\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function p(x)\ndef p(x):\n    return x**2 - 8*x + 5\n\n# Calculate p(3) and p(4)\np_3 = p(3)\np_4 = p(4)\n\n# Calculate the ratio p(3) / p(4)\nratio = p_3 / p_4\nprint((p_3, p_4, ratio))\n```", 'Let $f(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $3-\\sqrt{7}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{f(2)}{f(3)}.$\nLet $g(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{13}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{g(3)}{g(4)}.$\nLet $h(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $5-\\sqrt{15}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{h(4)}{h(5)}.$\nLet $q(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $6-\\sqrt{17}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{q(5)}{q(6)}.$\nLet $r(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $7-\\sqrt{19}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{r(6)}{r(7)}.$\nLet $s(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $8-\\sqrt{21}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{s(7)}{s(8)}.$\nLet $t(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $9-\\sqrt{23}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{t(8)}{t(9)}.$\nLet $u(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $10-\\sqrt{25}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{u(9)}{u(10)}.$\nLet $v(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $11-\\sqrt{27}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{v(10)}{v(11)}.$\nLet $w(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $12-\\sqrt{29}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{w(11)}{w(12)}.$\nLet $x(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $13-\\sqrt{31}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{x(12)}{x(13)}.$\nLet $y(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $14-\\sqrt{33}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{y(13)}{y(14)}.$\nLet $z(x)$ be a quadratic polynom