ratic formula \\(z = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\).\n\nFor the first equation \\(z^2 + 2zi - i = 0\\), we have \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = 2i\\), and \\(c = -i\\). The solutions are:\n\\[z = \\frac{-2i \\pm \\sqrt{(2i)^2 - 4(1)(-i)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{-2i \\pm \\sqrt{-4 + 4i}}{2} = \\frac{-2i \\pm 2\\sqrt{-1 + i}}{2} = -i \\pm \\sqrt{-1 + i}.\\]\n\nFor the second equation \\(z^2 + 2zi + 1 = 0\\), we have \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = 2i\\), and \\(c = 1\\). The solutions are:\n\\[z = \\frac{-2i \\pm \\sqrt{(2i)^2 - 4(1)(1)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{-2i \\pm \\sqrt{-4 - 4}}{2} = \\frac{-2i \\pm 2\\sqrt{-2}}{2} = -i \\pm \\sqrt{-2} = -i \\pm i\\sqrt{2}.\\]\n\nSo the roots of the polynomial are:\n\\[z = -i + \\sqrt{-1 + i},\\]\n\\[z = -i - \\sqrt{-1 + i},\\]\n\\[z = -i + i\\sqrt{2},\\]\n\\[z = -i - i\\sqrt{2}.\\]\n\nThese roots are the vertices of a convex polygon in the complex plane. To find the area of this polygon, we can use the Shoelace formula. The vertices in the complex plane are:\n\\[z_1 = -i + \\sqrt{-1 + i},\\]\n\\[z_2 = -i - \\sqrt{-1 + i},\\]\n\\[z_3 = -i + i\\sqrt{2},\\]\n\\[z_4 = -i - i\\sqrt{2}.\\]\n\nWe can convert these vertices to their real and imaginary parts and then use the Shoelace formula to find the area. Let's calculate this using Python.\n```python\nimport cmath\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# Define the roots\r\nz1 = -1j + cmath.sqrt(-1 + 1j)\r\nz2 = -1j - cmath.sqrt(-1 + 1j)\r\nz3 = -1j + 1j * cmath.sqrt(2)\r\nz4 = -1j - 1j * cmath.sqrt(2)\r\n\r\n# Extract real and imaginary parts\r\npoints = [(z1.real, z1.imag), (z2.real, z2.imag), (z3.real, z3.imag), (z4.real, z4.imag)]\r\n\r\n# Use the Shoelace formula to calculate the area\r\ndef shoelace_formula(points):\r\n    n = len(points)\r\n    area = 0.5 * abs(sum(points[i][0] * points[(i + 1) % n][1] - points[(i + 1) % n][0] * points[i][1] for i in range(n)))\r\n    return area\r\n\r\narea = shoelace_formula(points)\r\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n2.82842712474619\n```\nThe area of the convex polygon formed by t