and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party. We can break this down into manageable steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from the 14 senators.\n2. Subtract the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans or all Democrats.\n\nLet's use Python and SymPy to calculate this step-by-step.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\nfrom sympy.functions.combinatorial.numbers import binomial\n\n# Total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 senators\ntotal_ways = binomial(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 (all Republicans)\nways_all_republicans = binomial(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 (all Democrats)\nways_all_democrats = binomial(6, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party\nways_at_least_one_from_each_party = total_ways - ways_all_republicans - ways_all_democrats\n\nprint(ways_at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve the problem of forming a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee with 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, where the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. Specifically, we will calculate the total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee from the 14 senators and subtract the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans or entirely of Democrats.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee from 14 senators.\n2. Calculate the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans.\n3. Calculate the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Democrats.\n4. Subtract the sum of the number of all-Republican and all-Democrat subcommittees from the total number of subcommittees to get the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nfrom math import comb\n\n# Total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee from 14 senators\ntotal_subcommittees = comb(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans\nall_republicans = comb(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Democrats\nall_democrats = comb(6, 5)\n\n# Number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party\nat_least_one_from_each_party = total_subcommittees - all_republicans - all_democrats\nprint(at_least_one_from_each_party)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee with 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, where the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party. We can use the principle of complementary counting. Specifically, we will find the total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee and subtract the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans or entirely of Democrats.\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee from 14 members.\n2. Calculate the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee entirely from Republicans.\n3. Calculate the number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee entirely from Democrats.\n4. Subtract the sum of the number of all-Republican and all-Democrat subcommittees from the total number of subcommittees.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Total number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee from 14 members\ntotal_subcommittees = math.comb(14, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee entirely from Republicans\nall_republicans = math.comb(8, 5)\n\n# Number of ways to choose a 5-member subcommittee entirely from Democrats\nall_democrats = math.comb(6, 5)\n\n# Number of valid subcommittees (at least one member from each party)\nvalid_subcommittees = total_subcommittees - all_republicans - all_democrats\n\nprint(valid_subcommittees)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a group of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the condition that the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party. We can break this problem down by considering the different possible distributions of Republicans and Democrats in the subcommittee:\n\n1. 4 Republicans and 1 Democrat\n2. 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats\n3. 2 Republicans and 3 Democrats\n4. 1 Republican and 4 Democrats\n\nWe will calculate the number of ways to form each of these subcommittees and then sum them up.\n\nThe number of ways to choose $k$ members from a group of $n$ members is given by the binomial coefficient $\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$.\n\nLet's calculate each case:\n\n1. The number of ways to choose 4 Republicans from 8 and 1 Democrat from 6 is $\\binom{8}{4} \\cdot \\binom{6}{1}$.\n2. The number of ways to choose 3 Republicans from 8 and 2 Democrats from 6 is $\\binom{8}{3} \\cdot \\binom{6}{2}$.\n3. The number of ways to choose 2 Republicans from 8 and 3 Democrats from 6 is $\\binom{8}{2} \\cdot \\binom{6}{3}$.\n4. The number of ways to choose 1 Republican from 8 and 4 Democrats from 6 is $\\binom{8}{1} \\cdot \\binom{6}{4}$.\n\nFinally, we sum up these values to get the total number of ways to form the subcommittee.\n\nLet's compute this using Python.\n```python\nfrom math import comb\n\n# Calculate the number of ways for each case\nways_4R_1D = comb(8, 4) * comb(6, 1)\nways_3R_2D = comb(8, 3) * comb(6, 2)\nways_2R_3D = comb(8, 2) * comb(6, 3)\nways_1R_4D = comb(8, 1) * comb(6, 4)\n\n# Sum up all the ways\ntotal_ways = ways_4R_1D + ways_3R_2D + ways_2R_3D + ways_1R_4D\nprint(total_ways)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with at least one member from each party, is \\(\\boxed{1940}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to count the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party. We can break this down into manageable steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from the 14 members of the committee.\n2. Subtract the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans or all Democrats.\n\nThe total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{14}{5} \\). The number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 is \\( \\binom{8}{5} \\), and the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 is \\( \\binom{6}{5} \\).\n\nSo, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is:\n\\[ \\binom{14}{5} - \\binom{8}{5} - \\binom{6}{5} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python:\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the combinations\ntotal_ways = math.comb(14, 5)\nall_republicans = math.comb(8, 5)\nall_democrats = math.comb(6, 5)\n\n# Calculate the number of valid subcommittees\nvalid_subcommittees = total_ways - all_republicans - all_democrats\nprint(valid_subcommittees)\n```\n```output\n1940\n```\nThe numbe