icient using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to compute the binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{31}{28}$. The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{n}{k}$ is defined as the number of ways to choose $k$ elements from a set of $n$ elements, and it can be computed using the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$. So, we need to compute:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factorial terms:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\cdot 30 \\cdot 29 \\cdot 28!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\cdot 30 \\cdot 29}{3!} = \\frac{31 \\cdot 30 \\cdot 29}{3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{31 \\cdot 30 \\cdot 29}{6}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's compute this value using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", 'To compute $\\binom{31}{28}$, we can use the formula for combinations:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$, so:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6}\n\\]\n\nWe can compute this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the combination using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\ncombination = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(combination)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\binom{31}{28}$ is $\\boxed{4495}$.', "To solve \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that \\(\\dbi