 boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils. Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. Roslyn has a total of 10 boxes.\n2. Five of the boxes contain pencils.\n3. Four of the boxes contain pens.\n4. Two of the boxes contain both pens and pencils.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion and exclusion, the number of boxes that contain either pens or pencils or both is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Number of boxes with pens or pencils or both} = \\text{Number of boxes with pencils} + \\text{Number of boxes with pens} - \\text{Number of boxes with both} \\]\n\nSo, the number of boxes with either pens or pencils or both is:\n\n\\[ 5 + 4 - 2 = 7 \\]\n\nSince there are 10 boxes in total, the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is:\n\n\\[ 10 - 7 = 3 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Total number of boxes\ntotal_boxes = 10\n\n# Number of boxes with pencils\nboxes_with_pencils = 5\n\n# Number of boxes with pens\nboxes_with_pens = 4\n\n# Number of boxes with both pens and pencils\nboxes_with_both = 2\n\n# Number of boxes with either pens or pencils or both\nboxes_with_either_or_both = boxes_with_pencils + boxes_with_pens - boxes_with_both\n\n# Number of boxes with neither pens nor pencils\nboxes_with_neither = total_boxes - boxes_with_either_or_both\nprint(boxes_with_neither)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to assign 3 people to 5 different offices such that no two people share an office. This is a permutation problem where we are choosing 3 offices out of 5 and arranging 3 people in those offices.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 offices out of 5 is given by the permutation formula \\(P(n, k) = \\frac{n!}{(n-k)!}\\), where \\(n\\) is the total number of items to choose from, and \\(k\\) is the number of items to choose. Here, \\(n = 5\\) and \\(k = 3\\).\n\nThe formula for permutations \\(