sing Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the number of ways to choose 3 offices out of 5\nnum_ways_choose_offices = math.comb(5, 3)\n\n# Calculate the number of ways to arrange 3 people in those 3 offices\nnum_ways_arrange_people = math.factorial(3)\n\n# Total number of ways to assign 3 people to 5 different offices\ntotal_ways = num_ways_choose_offices * num_ways_arrange_people\nprint(total_ways)\n```\n```output\n60\n```\nThe total number of ways to assign 3 people to 5 different offices such that each person gets exactly one office is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).", 'To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to assign 3 people to 5 different offices, ensuring that no two people share an office.\n\n1. Understanding the Problem:\n   - There are 3 people and 5 offices.\n   - Each person must be assigned to exactly one office.\n   - No two people can share an office.\n\n2. Choosing the First Person:\n   - The first person has 5 options for offices to choose from.\n\n3. Choosing the Second Person:\n   - After the first person has chosen an office, the second person has 4 options left (since one office is already taken).\n\n4. Choosing the Third Person:\n   - After the first two people have chosen their offices, the third person has 3 options left.\n\n5. Calculating the Total Number of Ways:\n   - The total number of ways to assign the 3 people to the 5 offices is the product of the number of choices for each person.\n   - This can be calculated as:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 4 \\times 3\n     \\]\n\n6. Performing the Multiplication:\n   - Multiply the numbers:\n     \\[\n     5 \\times 4 = 20\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     20 \\times 3 = 60\n     \\]\n\n7. Conclusion:\n   - There are 60 different ways to assign 3 people to 5 different offices, ensuring that no two people share an office.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]', 'If no one shares an office, each of the 3 people can be assigned to any of the 5 offices. The first person h