ubstituting and simplifying, we will get a polynomial equation in terms of \\(x\\). We will then find the coefficients of this polynomial and determine the smallest possible value of \\(|a| + |b| + |c| + |d|\\).\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python using sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols(\'x\')\n\n# Define the expressions for cosines and sines\ncos_alpha = x\ncos_beta = 2*x\ncos_gamma = 3*x\nsin_alpha = sp.sqrt(1 - x**2)\nsin_beta = sp.sqrt(1 - (2*x)**2)\nsin_gamma = sp.sqrt(1 - (3*x)**2)\n\n# Use the cosine addition formula\ncos_alpha_beta_gamma = cos_alpha * cos_beta * cos_gamma - cos_alpha * sin_beta * sin_gamma - cos_beta * sin_alpha * sin_gamma - cos_gamma * sin_alpha * sin_beta\n\n# Set the equation cos(alpha + beta + gamma) = -1\nequation = sp.Eq(cos_alpha_beta_gamma, -1)\n\n# Simplify the equation\nsimplified_equation = sp.simplify(equation)\n\n# Solve the equation for x\nsolutions = sp.solve(simplified_equation, x)\n\n# Find the cubic polynomial that x satisfies\nfor sol in solutions:\n    if sol.is_real:\n        # Substitute the solution back into the original equation to find the polynomial\n        poly = sp.simplify(sp.expand(sp.together(sp.simplify(sp.cos(sp.acos(sol) + sp.acos(2*sol) + sp.acos(3*sol)) + 1))))\n        # Find the coefficients of the polynomial\n        coeffs = sp.Poly(poly, x).all_coeffs()\n        # Calculate the sum of the absolute values of the coefficients\n        result = sum(abs(coeff) for coeff in coeffs)\n        print(f"Coefficients: {coeffs}, Sum of absolute values: {result}")\n\n# Find the smallest possible value of |a| + |b| + |c| + |d|\nmin_result = min([sum(abs(coeff) for coeff in sp.Poly(poly, x).all_coeffs()) for poly in [sp.simplify(sp.expand(sp.together(sp.simplify(sp.cos(sp.acos(sol) + sp.acos(2*sol) + sp.acos(3*sol)) + 1)))) for sol in solutions if sol.is_real]])\nprint(min_result)\n```\n```output\nDone\n```\nThe output indicates that the code has successfully executed