 \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\times 53.25}{10} \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{159.75}{10} \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 15.975 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\nTo express this as a fraction, we note that $15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000}$. Simplifying this fraction:\n\\[\n15.975 = \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles / 10) * real_life_distance\n\n# Convert the map distance to a fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(map_distance_fraction)\n```\n```output\n639/40\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "We can start by setting up a proportion to solve the problem. We know that 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life. Let's denote the distance on the map as \\( x \\) inches. The proportion can be set up as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nFrom this proportion, we can solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{3 \\times 53.25}{10} \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nNow we can compute the value of \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{159.75}{10} = 15.975 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nTo express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\( 15.975 \\) is the same as \\( \\frac{15975}{1000} \\). We can simplify this fraction by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 25:\n\n\\[\n15.975 = \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nSo the distance between the buildings on the map is \\( \\frac{639}{40} \\) inches. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\r\n\r\n# Given values\r\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\r\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\r\n\r\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\r\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_distance) / 10\r\n\r\n# Convert to fraction\r\nfraction_distance = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\r\n\r\nprint(fraction_distance)\n```\n```output\n639/40\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "The map scale is 3 inches : 10 miles. This means that for every 10 miles in real life, the map shows it as 3 inches. To find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life, we can set up a proportion and solve for the unknown distance on the map.\n\nThe proportion is:\n\\[ \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{3 \\times 53.25}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{159.75}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\\[ x = 15.975 \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nExpressing 15.975 as a fraction:\n\\[ 15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the scale and the real-life distance\nscale_numerator = 3  # inches on the map\nscale_denominator = 10  # miles in real life\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = (scale_numerator * real_life_distance) / scale_denominator\n\n# Convert the map distance to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(map_distance_fraction)\n```\n```output\n639/40\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the scale of the map and then use it to convert the real-life distance into the map distance. The scale of the map is given as 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life. This means that for every 10 miles in real life, the distance on the map is 3 inches. Therefore, for every 1 mile in real life, the distance on the map is $\\frac{3}{10}$ inches.\n\nGiven that the real-life distance between the two buildings is 53.25 miles, we can calculate the distance on the map by multiplying 53.25 miles by the scale factor $\\frac{3}{10}$.\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\nscale_factor = 3 / 10  # inches per mile\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = real_life_distance * scale_factor\n\n# Convert the map distance to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint((map_distance, map_distance_fraction))\n```\n```output\n(15.974999999999998, Fraction(639, 40))\n```\nThe distance between the two buildings on the map is approximately 15.975 inches. When expressed as a fraction, this distance is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "We can solve this problem by setting up a proportion. Given that 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life, we can set up the following proportion to find the distance on the map for 53.25 miles in real life:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{160.25 \\text{ inches}}{10} = 16.025 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nTo express this a