s that for every 10 miles in real life, the distance on the map is 3 inches. We can express this as a ratio:\n\n\\[ \\text{Scale} = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nTo find the distance on the map for a real-life distance of 53.25 miles, we can set up a proportion:\n\n\\[ \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\nscale_numerator = 3  # inches\nscale_denominator = 10  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = (scale_numerator * real_life_distance) / scale_denominator\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\( 15.975 \\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\( 15.975 \\) is the same as \\( \\frac{15975}{1000} \\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000, which is 25. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 25, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\( \\frac{639}{40} \\) inches.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To determine the distance between the two buildings on the map, we can use the given ratio of the map distance to the real-life distance. The ratio provided is 3 inches on the map for every 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nThe steps to solve this problem are as follows:\n\n1. Set up the ratio of map distance to real-life distance.\n2. Use the ratio to find the map distance that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nLet's denote the map distance by \\(d\\) inches. The ratio can be written as:\n\\[ \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{d \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nTo find \\(d\\), we can cross-multiply and solve for \\(d\\):\n\\[ d = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Given ratio of map distance to real-life distance\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles in real life\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_life_distance) / 10\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe map distance corresponding to 53.25 miles in real life is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\(15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000}\\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nLet's simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{15975}{1000}\\) to its simplest form.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Numerator and denominator\nnumerator = 15975\ndenominator = 1000\n\n# Find the greatest common divisor\ngcd = math.gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // gcd\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // gcd\n\nsimplified_fraction = (simplified_numerator, simplified_denominator)\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```\n```output\n(639, 40)\n```\nThe simplified fraction for \\(15.975\\) inches is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\).\n\nThus, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use that scale to find the distance on the map that corresponds to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles.\n\nGiven:\n- 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life.\n\nFirst, we need to find out how many miles correspond to 1 inch on the map. This can be done by dividing 10 miles by 3 inches.\n\nNext, we use this scale to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life. We do this by dividing 53.25 miles by the scale factor (the number of miles per inch).\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_in_inches = 3\nreal_distance_in_miles = 10\nreal_distance_given_in_miles = 53.25\n\n# Calculate the scale factor (miles per inch)\nscale_factor = real_distance_in_miles / map_distance_in_inches\n\n# Calculate the map distance for the given real distance\nmap_distance_for_given_real_distance = real_distance_given_in_miles / scale_factor\n\n# Convert the result to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance_for_given_real_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint((map_distance_for_given_real_distance, map_distance_fraction))\n```\n```output\n(15.975, Fraction(639, 40))\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map, corresponding to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles, is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "We can set up a proportion to solve this problem. The proportion is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches on the map}}{10 \\text{ miles in real life}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches on the map}}{53.25 \\text{ miles in real life}}\n\\]\nWe can solve for \\(x\\) by cross-multiplying:\n\\[\n3 \\times 53.25 = 10 \\times x\n\\]\n\\[\n159.75 = 10x\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{159.75}{10}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 15.975\n\\]\nTo express this as a fraction, we note that \\(15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000}\\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000. The GCD of 15975 and 1000 is 25, so we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 25:\n\\[\n\\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\r\n\r\n# Given values\r\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches on the map\r\nr