gers less than 100 that are divisible by 3, 5, and 7 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).\n3. The area of the largest rectangle with a perimeter of 48 cm and integer side lengths is \\(\\boxed{144}\\) square centimeters.\n4. The value of \\(x\\) in the rectangle divided into four smaller rectangles with areas 45, 50, 40, and \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{1500}\\).\n5. The largest prime divisor of the sum of all prime numbers between 1 and 100 is \\(\\boxed{53}\\).\n6. The area of the quadrilateral AEFB is \\(\\boxed{82}\\) square centimeters.\n7. The number of digits in \\(16^{16}\\) is \\(x = 33\\), the number of digits in \\(2^{3^4}\\) is \\(y = 49\\), and the number of digits in \\(3^{2^3}\\) is \\(z = 9\\). The largest of these is \\(y = 49\\), so the answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).\n8. The area of the quadrilateral AEFB is \\(\\boxed{82}\\) square centimeters.\n\nThe final answer for the area of the quadrilateral AEFB is \\(\\boxed{82}\\).", 'The diagram below shows two squares.  The total area of the two squares is 185 cm$^2$.  The difference in the side lengths of the two squares is 3 cm.  What is the side length of the larger square?  (Note that the diagram is not drawn to scale.)  \\begin{asy}\ndraw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle);\ndraw((10,0)--(17,0)--(17,7)--(10,7)--cycle);\nlabel("10 cm",(5,10),N);\nlabel("10 cm",(0,5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(17,3.5),E);\nlabel("10 cm",(8.5,0),S);\nlabel("7 cm",(17,3.5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(13.5,7),N);\n[/asy] \\begin{asy}\ndraw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle);\ndraw((10,0)--(17,0)--(17,7)--(10,7)--cycle);\nlabel("10 cm",(5,10),N);\nlabel("10 cm",(0,5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(17,3.5),E);\nlabel("10 cm",(8.5,0),S);\nlabel("7 cm",(17,3.5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(13.5,7),N);\n[/asy] \\begin{asy}\ndraw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle);\ndraw((10,0)--(17,0)--(17,7)--(10,7)--cycle);\nlabel("10 cm",(5,10),N);\nlabel("10 cm",(0,5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(17,3.5),E);\nlabel("10 cm",(8.5,0),S);\nlabel("7 cm",(17,3.5),W);\nlabel("10 cm",(13.5,7),N);\n[/as