ion at the given points\npi_over_3 = math.pi / 3\nsqrt_45 = math.sqrt(45)\neight_two_thirds = 8 ** (2/3)\n\n# Calculate the values\nf_pi_over_3 = f(pi_over_3)\nf_sqrt_45 = f(sqrt_45)\nf_eight_two_thirds = f(eight_two_thirds)\n\n# Sum the values\nresult = f_pi_over_3 + f_sqrt_45 + f_eight_two_thirds\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Sum up the total amount of money earned by Linda, Sherry, June, and Connie.\n2. Convert the total amount of money into cents.\n3. Determine how much money is left after converting as many of the coins into bills as possible (i.e., finding the remainder when the total amount in cents is divided by 100).\n\nLet's start by calculating the total amount of money in dollars and then convert it to cents. Finally, we'll find the remainder when this total is divided by 100.\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these steps:\n```python\n# Amounts earned by each girl scout in dollars\nlinda_earned = 27.47\nsherry_earned = 35.23\njune_earned = 37.37\nconnie_earned = 26.52\n\n# Total amount earned\ntotal_dollars = linda_earned + sherry_earned + june_earned + connie_earned\n\n# Convert total amount to cents (1 dollar = 100 cents)\ntotal_cents = int(total_dollars * 100)\n\n# Find the remainder when total_cents is divided by 100\nremaining_cents = total_cents % 100\n\nprint(remaining_cents)\n```\n```output\n59\n```\nAfter converting the total amount of money into cents and finding the remainder when divided by 100, the amount of money left after they converted as many of the coins into bills as they could is \\(\\boxed{59}\\) cents.", "To determine the amount of money left after converting as many coins as possible into bills, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of money earned by the girls.\n2. Convert this total amount into cents.\n3. Determine the remainder when this total amount is divided by 100 (since there are 10