 of all the students and then divide it by the number of students. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 80.\n2. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 90.\n3. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 100.\n4. Sum these total scores to get the overall total score.\n5. Divide the overall total score by the number of students to get the class average.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step in Python.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\nscore_80 = 80\nscore_90 = 90\nscore_100 = 100\n\n# Calculate the total score for each group of students\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * score_80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * score_90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * score_100\n\n# Calculate the overall total score\noverall_total_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Calculate the class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.66666666666667\n```\nThe class average on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.67}\\).", 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a time of $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ into an improper fraction. The mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ is equivalent to $\\frac{11}{4}$.\n\nNow we can substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction $\\frac{550}{4}$ by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction $\\frac{275}{2}$ to a mixed number. To do this, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part, and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo the mixed number is $137\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTherefore, the car would travel $137\\frac{1}{2}$ miles in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours (which is 2 3/4 hours)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/2"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', 'To determine how far a car would travel at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance traveled:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to its simplest form. We can do this by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_part\nfraction_numerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part} {fraction_numerator}/2"\n\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', 'To determine how far a car travels at 50 miles per hour in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2\\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nTo express the answer as a mixed number, we need to divide 550 by 4 to get the whole number part and the remainder will give us the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is \\(137\\frac{2}{4}\\). We can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nnumerator //= common_divisor\ndenominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Display the mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number}{numerator}/{denominator}" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n1371/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', 'To determine how far a car would travel at a speed of 50 miles per hour in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ to an improper fraction. \n\n\\[ 2\\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction $\\frac{275}{2}$ to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the car would travel $137\\frac{1}{2}$ miles in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nfraction_numerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part}{fraction_numerator}/2"\n\nprint(mixed_number)\n```', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for a duration of \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2\\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo the distance traveled is \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_part\nfraction_numerator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[0]\nfraction_denominator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[1]\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(fraction_numerator, fraction_denominator)\nsimplified_numerator = fraction_numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = fraction_denominator // common_divisor\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part} {simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_numerator != 0 else f"{whole_part}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe distance traveled by the car at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours is \\(\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the spee