ct \\(ab = \\sqrt{(x + \\sqrt{3x + 6})(x - \\sqrt{3x + 6})} = \\sqrt{x^2 - (3x + 6)} = \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6}\\).\n6. Substituting \\(ab = \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6}\\) into the equation \\(x + ab = 18\\) gives us \\(x + \\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6} = 18\\).\n7. Isolating the square root term, we get \\(\\sqrt{x^2 - 3x - 6} = 18 - x\\). Squaring both sides gives us \\(x^2 - 3x - 6 = (18 - x)^2 = 324 - 36x + x^2\\).\n8. Simplifying the equation \\(x^2 - 3x - 6 = 324 - 36x + x^2\\) gives us \\(33x - 330 = 0\\), or \\(33x = 330\\), so \\(x = 10\\).\n\nWe can verify this solution by substituting \\(x = 10\\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true. Let's do this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the function for the original equation\ndef original_equation(x):\n    term1 = math.sqrt(x + math.sqrt(3 * x + 6))\n    term2 = math.sqrt(x - math.sqrt(3 * x + 6))\n    return term1 + term2\n\n# Check the value of the equation when x = 10\nx = 10\nresult = original_equation(x)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n6.0\n```\nThe value of the original equation when \\(x = 10\\) is indeed 6, confirming that our solution is correct. Therefore, the solution to the equation \\(\\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} + \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}} = 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} + \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}} = 6\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\(a = \\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\) and \\(b = \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\). Then the equation becomes \\(a + b = 6\\).\n2. Square both sides of the equation \\(a + b = 6\\) to get \\(a^2 + b^2 + 2ab = 36\\).\n3. Substitute \\(a^2 = x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}\\) and \\(b^2 = x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}\\) into the equation. This gives us \\(a^2 + b^2 = (x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}) + (x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}) = 2x\\).\n4. So the equation becomes \\(2x + 2ab = 36\\), which simplifies to \\(x + ab = 18\\).\n5. Since \\(a = \\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\) and \\(b = \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\), we have \\(ab = \\sqrt{(