alities)\n```\n```output\n48\n```\nThe total number of different personalities Tom can create with his Mr. Potato Head is \\(\\boxed{48}\\).", "To determine the number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with, we need to consider all the possible combinations of the available parts. Here's the breakdown of the parts and their respective options:\n\n- 3 hairstyles (including bald)\n- 2 sets of eyebrows\n- 1 pair of googly eyes\n- 2 sets of ears\n- 2 sets of lips\n- 2 pairs of shoes (regular and clown)\n\nSince each part can be chosen independently, the total number of different personalities can be calculated by multiplying the number of choices for each part together. The formula is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total Personalities} = (\\text{Number of hairstyles}) \\times (\\text{Number of eyebrow sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of eye options}) \\times (\\text{Number of ear sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of lip sets}) \\times (\\text{Number of shoe pairs}) \\]\n\nPlugging in the numbers:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total Personalities} = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the number of options for each part\nnum_head_styles = 3\nnum_eyebrow_sets = 2\nnum_eyes = 1\nnum_ear_sets = 2\nnum_lip_sets = 2\nnum_shoe_pairs = 2\n\n# Calculate the total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = (num_head_styles * \n                       num_eyebrow_sets * \n                       num_eyes * \n                       num_ear_sets * \n                       num_lip_sets * \n                       num_shoe_pairs)\n\nprint(total_personalities)\n```\n```output\n48\n```\nThe total number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with is \\(\\boxed{48}\\).", "To determine the number of different personalities Tom can create with his Mr. Potato Head, we need to consider all the possible combinations of the available parts. Here's the breakdown of the parts and their possible combina